<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Making a checklist">
        <ol>
            <li>Open <a href="/manage/checklists">Checklists</a> and press <strong>New checklist</strong>.</li>
            <li>Give it a <strong>Name</strong>, such as Opening, and an optional <strong>Description</strong>.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Runs on</strong>, tap the days it runs. <strong>Every day</strong>, <strong>Weekdays</strong>
                and <strong>Weekends</strong> pick those days in one go.</li>
            <li>Leave <strong>Skip days the location is closed</strong> ticked so it doesn't run on a day with no opening
                hours. A location with no opening hours set up at all counts as open every day. A day marked closed under
                Rota &gt; Holidays is always skipped.</li>
            <li>Choose when it's <strong>Due</strong> (see below) and press <strong>Create checklist</strong>.</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Add task</strong> for each task, in the order they're done.</li>
        </ol>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="When it's due">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>After opening</strong>: a number of minutes after the location opens that day, such as 15 minutes
                after opening.</li>
            <li><strong>Before closing</strong>: a number of minutes before the location closes that day. Use 0 for "by
                closing time". If the location closes after midnight, that counts as the same day.</li>
            <li><strong>At a set time</strong>: a time of day, such as 10:00.</li>
            <li><strong>No set time</strong>: it only counts as missed if the day ends with tasks still to tick.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            Opening and closing times come from the location's opening hours, which an Admin sets under Companies &amp;
            Locations. On a day with no opening hours, an opening or closing checklist has no due time.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Who can tick it">
        <FluentText>
            By default anyone on that day's rota at the location can tick the tasks, and so can its Managers and Admins.
            Choose a position under <strong>Who can tick it</strong> to limit it to people who hold that position, such as
            Duty Manager for Closing.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Tasks">
        <ul>
            <li>Each task has a title and optional details, such as where the keys are kept.</li>
            <li><strong>Ticking it asks for</strong>: <strong>Just a tick</strong>; <strong>A tick, with an optional
                note</strong>; or <strong>A number reading</strong>, with an optional unit such as °C for a fridge
                temperature.</li>
            <li>A number reading can have an <strong>Acceptable range (optional)</strong>: a <strong>Lowest
                acceptable</strong>, a <strong>Highest acceptable</strong>, or both. Leave one blank for an open end, such as
                only a highest of 5 °C for a fridge. Both ends count as acceptable.</li>
            <li>With a range set, choose <strong>When a reading is outside the range</strong>: <strong>Raise an alert and
                notify Managers</strong> (an Operations Alert plus a push to the location's Managers and the Admins),
                <strong>Raise an alert only</strong>, or <strong>Don't alert, just flag it on the task</strong>. A reading
                outside the range is always flagged on the task, whichever you choose.</li>
            <li>Use the up and down arrows to change the order, the pencil to edit a task, and the bin to remove it.</li>
            <li>Changes apply from the next day the checklist runs. Today's tasks change too, as long as nobody has ticked
                anything yet today. A reading is always judged against the range the task had on that day, so changing a
                range never changes past days.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
